  "implementation": {
    "world": "FPSWorld caches native grass/tree rows, transforms, bounds and spatial priorities. Bounded grass selection, partial far selection, tree LOD/culling, compact bulk instance uploads, terrain sample generation, atlas payloads, residency planning and terrain visibility are native. Terrain worker count remains two; uploads now have an 800 us admission budget in addition to the two-upload cap.",
    "motion": "FPSMovement supplies native CS client prediction/collision/stairs, correction sweeps and batched vehicle interpolation. Authority and prediction share CS horizontal math and the stair collision helper. Jetpack prediction reuses authority Jetpack tick/moved. Scene/input/seat presentation remains Godot-owned.",
    "destruction": "FPSDestruction owns packed cell/column/topology data, candidate ordering, support status and baked-attribute-preserving mesh patch generation. Immutable mesh sources decode during loading. One worker job at a time, per-site revision coalescing, round-generation rejection and owner-thread visual commits; gameplay and collision update immediately.",
    "animation": "Unchanged; optional follow-up contingent on profiling."
  },
  "remaining_script_work": [
    "Authored landscape/road setup and tree/grass candidate generation within terrain workers.",
    "Godot task scheduling, texture and mesh resource commits, scene construction and collision-node lifecycle.",
    "Input collection, room-scale orchestration, prediction history/reconciliation bookkeeping and vehicle presentation wiring.",
    "Authored structural graph setup, reliable destruction replication and cosmetic effect orchestration."
